## customerCode construction (current) and everything derived from it

### 1. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` — builds `customerCode`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`

Format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`; sequence = per-city owner count + 1.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String city = owner.getCity();
    int sequence = (int) OwnerCity.countOwnersInCity(ownerRepository, city) + 1;
    owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d",
            first3Upper(city), first3Upper(owner.getLastName()), sequence));
}
private static String first3Upper(String s) {
    return s.substring(0, Math.min(3, s.length())).toUpperCase();
}
```

### 2. `OwnerCity` — the per-city sequence source (also used by capacity check)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerCity.java`
```java
static long countOwnersInCity(OwnerRepository ownerRepository, String city) {
    return ownerRepository.findAll().stream()
            .filter(existing -> city.equals(existing.getCity()))
            .count();
}
```
"Same city" is an exact match. Shared with `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` so the sequence and capacity count stay consistent.

### 3. `AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` — derived from customerCode + registration year
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerMembershipNumber.java`

Format `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    String yy = String.format("%02d", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);
    owner.setMembershipNumber(String.format("%s-M%s", owner.getCustomerCode(), yy));
}
```
The `YY` comes from `registrationDate`, which is set in `BuildOwner` via `BusinessDays.effectiveRegistrationDate(...)`.

### 4. `OwnerCheckDigit` — the membership/customer-code check digit (Luhn)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerCheckDigit.java`

Read-time Luhn over the digits in `customerCode`; no stored column.
```java
public static Integer checkDigit(Owner owner) {
    return luhn(owner.getCustomerCode());
}
public static Integer luhn(String s) {
    if (s == null) return null;
    int sum = 0;
    boolean dbl = true;
    for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        char c = s.charAt(i);
        if (c < '0' || c > '9') continue;
        int d = c - '0';
        if (dbl) { d *= 2; if (d > 9) d -= 9; }
        sum += d;
        dbl = !dbl;
    }
    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```
Exposed on the DTO through `OwnerMapper.checkDigit`. (The acceptance test base has an identical `luhn`.)

### 5. `AuditOwnerCreated` — the create audit record
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`

Emits an audit line (carrying `customerCode`) on the `AUDIT` logger after save.
```java
private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
            owner.getMembershipLevel());
}
```
Asserted in tests via `AuditLogCapture` (captures the `AUDIT` Logback logger).

