## normalizedTelephone / telephone normalization

### `OwnerTelephone` — E.164 normalization
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java`
```java
static String toE164(String value) {
    if (value == null) return null;
    String cleaned = value.replaceAll("[\\s()\\-]", "");
    String digits;
    if (cleaned.startsWith("+")) {
        digits = cleaned.substring(1);
    } else {
        String national = cleaned.startsWith("0") ? cleaned.substring(1) : cleaned;
        digits = "61" + national;
    }
    if (!digits.matches("[0-9]{8,15}")) return null;
    for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : NATIONAL_LENGTH.entrySet()) {
        String code = entry.getKey();
        if (digits.startsWith(code)) {
            int nationalLength = digits.length() - code.length();
            return nationalLength == entry.getValue() ? "+" + digits : null;
        }
    }
    return "+" + digits;
}
```
`NATIONAL_LENGTH` = `{61→9, 1→10}` (LinkedHashMap, longest-code-first). Used by `ValidateOwnerFields` (replaces the submitted value) and by `OwnerIdentity` (builds the comparison key) so they can't drift. The `Owner.telephone` field also carries a bean-validation `@Pattern("^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$")`.

