## SHA-256 hashing

### `OwnerHousehold` — SHA-256 household id (the only production SHA-256 today)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerHousehold.java`

`householdId` = `"HH-"` + first 12 UPPER-hex chars (6 bytes) of SHA-256 of normalized `"<lastName>|<address>"`.
```java
static String householdId(String lastName, String address) {
    String key = normalize(lastName) + "|" + OwnerAddress.normalize(address);
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
                .digest(key.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < 6; i++) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02X", digest[i]));
        }
        return "HH-" + sb;
    } catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException ex) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", ex);
    }
}
static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) return "";
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
static boolean sameHousehold(Owner existing, String lastName, String address) {
    return normalize(existing.getLastName()).equals(normalize(lastName))
            && OwnerAddress.normalize(existing.getAddress())
                    .equals(OwnerAddress.normalize(address));
}
```
This is the pattern the redesigned `customerCode` `<HASH8>` will likely mirror (the test base's `shaHex(s, n)` returns the first n UPPER-hex of SHA-256, and `sha256hex` the full lower-hex). The test base holds the only SHA-256 code on the test side.

---

## Owner identity key (duplicate detection) — related, telephone+SHA both feed it

### `OwnerIdentity` — builds `identityKey`
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentity.java`

Key = `normalizedTelephone + "|" + email + "|" + householdId`.
```java
public static String identityKey(String telephone, String email, String householdId) {
    String normalizedTelephone = OwnerTelephone.toE164(telephone);
    String normalizedEmail = OwnerEmail.normalize(email);
    return (normalizedTelephone == null ? "" : normalizedTelephone) + "|"
            + (normalizedEmail == null ? "" : normalizedEmail) + "|"
            + (householdId == null ? "" : householdId);
}
public static String identityKey(Owner owner) {
    return identityKey(owner.getTelephone(), owner.getEmail(), owner.getHouseholdId());
}
static String forRequest(OwnerFieldsDto request) {
    String householdId = Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())
            ? OwnerHousehold.householdId(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress())
            : "";
    return identityKey(request.getTelephone(), request.getEmail(), householdId);
}
```
Enforced by `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` (throws `OwnerIdentityDuplicateException` → 409); exposed on the DTO via `OwnerMapper.identityKey`.

Supporting helpers:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerEmail.java` — `isValid` + `normalize` (lower-case).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerAddress.java` — address `normalize` (collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/AssignOwnerHousehold.java` — assigns/back-fills `householdId`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerIdentityDuplicateException.java` and `...ExceptionHandler.java`.

