## Read-time projection onto the DTO

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

MapStruct mapper; derives `checkDigit`, `identityKey`, `locality` (plus `displayName`, `initials`, `contactPreference`) at read time:
```java
@Mapping(target = "locality",    source = "owner", qualifiedByName = "locality")
@Mapping(target = "identityKey", source = "owner", qualifiedByName = "identityKey")
@Mapping(target = "checkDigit",  source = "owner", qualifiedByName = "checkDigit")
OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);

default Integer checkDigit(Owner owner) { return OwnerCheckDigit.checkDigit(owner); }
default String identityKey(Owner owner) { return OwnerIdentity.identityKey(owner); }
default String locality(Owner owner) { return OwnerRegion.localityOf(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode()); }
```

## Owner entity (persisted fields)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

Stored columns relevant here: `customer_code`, `membership_number`, `household_id`, `household_size`, `namesake_count`, `membership_level`, `bulk_signup_warning`, `postcode`, `registration_date`, `telephone` (with E.164 `@Pattern`), `email`, `city`, `address`. `checkDigit`, `identityKey`, `locality` are **not** stored — derived at read time.

## Create pipeline order (POST /api/owners)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

`validate (ValidateOwnerFields)` → `checkIdentity (CheckOwnerIdentityUnique)` → `checkCityCapacity` → `checkDailyLimit` → `build (BuildOwner)` → `assignHousehold` → `countHousehold` → **`assignCustomerCode`** → **`assignMembershipNumber`** → `countNamesakes` → `assignMembershipLevel` → `flagBulkSignup` → `save` → **`audit (AuditOwnerCreated)`** → `respond`. Authorized by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

Supporting pipeline files (relevant to identity assembly):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java` — normalizes telephone (E.164), address, email; validates postcode via `OwnerRegion.isPostcodeValid`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/BuildOwner.java` — maps DTO→Owner, sets effective `registrationDate` via `BusinessDays`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/BusinessDays.java` — `effectiveRegistrationDate` (weekend roll) feeds the membership-number `YY`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/CountOwnerNamesakes.java`, `AssignOwnerMembershipLevel.java` — feed the audit record's `membershipLevel`.
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/ApplyOwner.java`, `SaveOwner.java`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`.

## OpenAPI contract
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (lines ~2104-2196) documents `customerCode` (`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`), `checkDigit` (Luhn over customerCode), `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `householdId` (`HH-` + hash), `identityKey`, and `locality`. These descriptions describe the CURRENT format and will need updating when `customerCode` becomes `<REGION>-<HASH8>`.

## Tests related to owner identity
All tests are black-box acceptance tests under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`:
- `AcceptanceTest.java` — the pending redesign assertion (`customerCode` must match `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`).
- `AcceptanceBase.java` — infra + ground-truth tables and the reference algorithms the tests assert against: `sha256hex`, `shaHex(s,n)` (first n UPPER-hex), `luhn`, `region(city)`, `CITY_REGION`, `REGION_POSTCODES`, `REGION_TIMEZONE`, `validPostcode`, `knownOwner`, `withPostcode`, business-day roll, `@Transactional` + `@WithMockUser(OWNER_ADMIN)`.
- `AuditLogCapture.java` — captures the `AUDIT` logger (used to assert `AuditOwnerCreated`).

No unit tests exist for the individual function classes; the redesign is validated purely through the acceptance suite.

